  "player_hint_1_en": "Using the general clue (\"No one was beside a table.\"), some squares are ruled out for Cora. So Cora (C) must be at row 3, column 3. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_2_en": "Alma can't be at row 2, column 7; row 5, column 8: in each case Edith's clue (\"There was a man in her area.\") could not be true. Suppose Faye were at row 4, column 6: then Holly would have nowhere left to go. So Faye can't be there. Testing the remaining squares the same way rules out a few more. So Alma (A) must be at row 4, column 9. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_3_en": "With the rows and columns of Cora and Alma crossed out, only one square is left for Holly that fits her clue (\"She was beside a speaker in the Stage.\"). So Holly (H) must be at row 1, column 8. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_4_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Bella that fits her clue (\"She was the only person beside a drum set.\"). So Bella (B) must be at row 2, column 4. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_5_en": "Suppose Faye were at row 6, column 7: then Edith's clue (\"There was a man in her area.\") could not be true. So Faye can't be there. Faye's own clue (\"Someone else in her area was sitting in a chair. She was north of Valerie.\") rules out more squares. So Faye (F) must be at row 5, column 6. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_6_en": "Suppose Duncan were at row 9, column 2: then nobody could stand in column 1. So Duncan can't be there. Gus can't be at row 8, column 1; row 8, column 5: in each case Edith would have nowhere left to go. So Duncan (D) must be at row 8, column 1. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_7_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Gus that fits his clue (\"He was exactly one row north of Duncan.\"). So Gus (G) must be at row 7, column 5. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_8_en": "Valerie is now the only person who can still go in row 6. So Valerie (the victim) must be at row 6, column 7. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_9_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Edith that fits her clue (\"There was a man in her area.\"). So Edith (E) must be at row 9, column 2. Cross out her row and column. Faye is the only person in the Orchestra Pit with Valerie, so Faye is the murderer!"
 },
